        "jsCode": "// Get the input data (works for any structure)\nconst inputData = $input.first().json;\n\n// Check if 'pages' exists and is an array\nif (inputData.pages && Array.isArray(inputData.pages)) {\n  const combinedText = inputData.pages\n    .map(page => page.markdown || \"\") // Get markdown or empty string if missing\n    .filter(text => text !== \"\")      // Remove empty pages\n    .join('\\n\\n');                    // Combine with double newlines\n\n  return {\n    combined_markdown: combinedText\n  };\n}\n\n// Fallback if the input doesn't have a 'pages' array\nreturn {\n  error: \"No 'pages' array found in the input data\",\n  combined_markdown: \"\"\n};"
